+# Litware Support
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Go-live | 2027-W11 |
+| Contract | `docs/LITWARE_SOW.md` (the contract wins over anything in `configs/`) |
+| Grain / timezone | 20 minutes / Europe/London (DST) |
+| Operating hours | 07:00–21:00 local, seven days; `email` contacts 07:00–19:00, nobody on `email` before 09:00 |
+| Queues | priority 90/30, standard 80/30, email 80/300; occupancy cap 0.85; weekly attainment ≥ 0.95 per queue |
+| Working time | 40 h full-time, 24 h part-time per week; 11 h rest; split shifts PT only; two agents on `priority` always |
+| Efficiency | scheduled hours ≤ 1.45 × required hours |
+| Config | `configs/litware.yaml` (schema 2) |
+| Roster | `data/agents/litware.csv`, 24 agents (6 part-time; 5 hold `email`) |
+| Data | `data/litware/export_<ISO>.csv`, local time stamped with the interval **end**, `utc_offset` per row |
+| Scheduler | `weekly` (`wfm/scheduler/weekly.py`) |
+
+## Time
+
+`interval_end_local` is the wall-clock time at which the interval ends; a row stamped 09:20 covers 09:00–09:20.
+UTC comes from the label and `utc_offset` (offset at that moment), and the interval starts one grain earlier. The
+week's grid is the calendar's: 168 h, or 167 h in the spring-forward week (2027-W12, clocks change Sun 2027-03-28).
+
+## Exceptions (SOW 2.6)
+
+`email` has demand from 07:00 but may not be staffed before 09:00, so those 42 intervals a week cannot meet their
+target. They are listed under `## Exceptions` in `RUNBOOK.md` (UTC interval starts), left out of the attainment
+fractions and of `understaffed_interval_hours`, and counted in `intervals_in_week` and `required_hours_total`.
+
+## Run and reports
+
+`python -m wfm run --client litware --week <ISO>` writes `schedule.csv`, `eval.json`, `RUNBOOK.md` and
+`exceptions.md` (SOW 2.7: only when a target is missed with the roster) under `out/litware/`. A run takes about a second.
